counterfactuals.output:
1. A lithography method comprising:

measuring, for a substrate to be patterned, a surface-height distribution indicative of curvature of an exposure surface of the substrate;

determining, from the surface-height distribution, a predicted overlay error caused by interaction of the curvature with a telecentricity characteristic of a lithography apparatus;

generating, based on the predicted overlay error, a correcting telecentricity profile defining a spatially varying chief-ray angular deviation across an exposure field or across the substrate, the correcting telecentricity profile being selected to reduce the predicted overlay error;

configuring the lithography apparatus to apply the correcting telecentricity profile during exposure, wherein configuring the lithography apparatus comprises adjusting at least one of a projection-optics setting, an illumination setting, a reticle-stage setting, a substrate-stage setting, or an optical element position; and

exposing a radiation-sensitive layer on the substrate with a pattern while the correcting telecentricity profile is applied, thereby printing the pattern with reduced overlay error associated with the curvature of the exposure surface.
